From 670095bcc5f388f7f6c78ab34c86672fc162257f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:57:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Compare consecutive quarters only on one presentation
 basis

When a year-to-date figure ends on the quarter, the previous cumulative figure plus the
quarter must add up to it (within printed rounding); otherwise a re-presentation, such
as a business moved to discontinued operations, put the two quarters on different bases
and the quarter-over-quarter change is withheld.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CfTpoii6QDStyTPdotmEdY
